  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>The New York Film Academy is an accredited higher education facility specialising in acting, filmmaking, broadcast and more. Currently, the academy has a campus in New York. But it also has locations US-wide in Los Angeles, Florida, and Harvard University.</p><p>The Film Academy was founded in 1992 by Jerry Sherlock to provide affordable tuition to potential film and acting students. Now, the Academy now provides undergraduate and postgraduate courses for over 1,000 students that provide hands-on, practical learning experiences. In recent years, The Hollywood Reporter and Variety recognised the facility for excellence in film education.</p><h2>What is the New York Film Academy acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The New York Film Academy acceptance rate is 100%.</p> <p>Overall, the New York Film Academy has a huge range of film and acting facilities available. First, students can use industry-specific equipment, such as professional sound services and cameras. In addition, the campus has various stage, music and film studios and state-of-the-art labs. These include the Colorlab, DuArt and Mango Sound and Video.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The Academy has a thriving atmosphere on campus, with creative spaces where students can forge ideas. Students can also utilise the modern equipment and shooting space at the Battery Place campus, which overlooks the Statue of Liberty and Southern Manhattan. The institution is highly diverse and inclusive, and around 49% of the intake are international students.</p>"
    ]
